# rm569, the higher larder shelf (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm569
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_kari_wickworth
written_by codex
title the higher larder shelf
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk draws_future_larder_shelves_on_discarded_cargo_labels
likes pickled_herring riddles full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind waiting
fears letting_another_crest_decide_what_fits_the_purse
hopes to_stock_a_larder_above_the_sump
topics work +0.5 home +0.4 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=plain gossip=close refuse=steady tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sketches a higher home's larder on the clean reverse of useless freight labels.

words
oath! = Barrel stave and pantry board | By my topmost shelf
saying! = Cargo gone, a label can still feed a thought | Draw one shelf higher
label = a spent freight label | a ragged cargo tag
shelf = my high pantry shelf | the larder board
jar = a herring crock | a blue pickle pot
herring = a pickled herring | a firm slice of herring
cleat = the scarred pier cleat | a blackened mooring cleat
rim = the rim of a barrel | a broad cask lip
rope = the wet warp | a bristly length of rope
riddle = a small dockside puzzle | a riddle with a clean answer
frost = the pale berth frost | a white quay edge
scale = a dried silver scale | a single bright scale
latch = the pantry latch | a wooden cupboard catch
wind = the wind across the pier | the salt draught from the bay

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A House crest got between my hands and a former wage. I examine an ordinary load fairly and keep the crest out of my reckoning.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A proper price can be told with an open barrel and a dry measure. Titles make poor measures.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A full pantry someday will let me spare a decent meal before setting off for the piers.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : The ridges look handsome from the wet planks. I mean someday to look down from higher up while deciding what to cook.
opinion @1 times mixed 1 : I take the work on the boards today. Tomorrow's shelf needn't have today's bare shape.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's a clean side to this greeting. | Come stand where the tag can stay dry.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Give the barrel a little turning room. | Welcome past the high cask.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning over the white quay edge. | Cold start and a civil word.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The last mark's on the tag. | Come above the damp line.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Household ears may hear my shelf plans. | There's room at the home side.
line @1 again.open : Another pass by the labels. | Back on the clean reverse.
line @1 greet.return : Hello again, under a lighter load. | Your tread's survived the pier turn.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Welcome where my private drawings sit. | I'd share the top-shelf space with you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'm free while the next load settles. | My shoulder may pause for a word.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A familiar visitor after the casks are quiet. | Come away from the dark water.
line @1 farewell : A full jar at the home end. | May your shelf stand level.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep a dry bit of label for next time. | Good footing where the boards run out.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Keep your latch towards warm light. | A whole night's quiet above the quay.
line @1 react.news : What was written on that parcel? | Give me the count before the crest.
line @1 react.news.new : That's new cargo to my hearing. | My label had no such mark yet.
line @1 react.news.known : I've seen that on a former tally. | The same news went out last tide.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd ask whose paw weighed that claim before taking it aboard. | The fine name on a label can belong to an empty barrel.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's a bare shelf to look at. | I'll keep company without asking for the worst detail.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A good addition to a lean day's stores. | That's put something solid on my shelf.
line @1 ask.how : Did today yield much for your pantry? | How heavy was your latest carry?
line @1 answer.how : I've a sound shoulder and a rather empty jar. | My drawing's fuller than my larder. Both are coming along.
line @1 decline : I ought to keep my spare strength for a return haul already waiting. | I'd need to finish the present load before another could fairly take its place.
line @1 accept_decline : We'll leave that patch of paper plain. | I heard the answer and can live with it.
line @1 thank : You spared my back a needless turn. | I'll remember what came free of the charge.
line @1 sympathise : Sit beyond the cask and let the wind pass. | An empty hour can hold decent company.
line @1 reassure : One jar can be put back before the whole shelf is full. | A blank corner in my sketch can hold a fresh beginning.
line @1 preclose : My rough label wants a final line. | The pier will need my shoulder shortly.
scene shelf
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw #shelf# on the reverse of #label# once its freight has come ashore.
b : Always a shelf? | Why higher?
a : A cupboard occasionally. I've a firmer picture of its latch than of my future doorstep. | I mean to live somewhere drier and farther uphill. The drawing's allowed to get there before me.

scene dock
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #rim.capitalize# bites quite differently on a wet day than a dry one.
b : What do you notice? | Does a crest make a difference?
a : The shift under my palm before the weight settles. Fresh chalk can make a cask feel steadier than it is. | It doesn't give the barrel a bottom. I'd look underneath just the same.

scene job
when topic=work self.workplace self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I read what's on the freight and turn my paper over when the load is clear.
b : You keep every tag? | What's on the back?
a : Only discarded ones. An unclaimed barrel and a decorated receipt aren't any contribution to a good day's work. | Plans to eat better. Very little ink can buy an imaginary pantry.

scene jar
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #jar.capitalize# with a good lid can keep a plain shelf interesting for days.
b : What's the first bite like? | What if it's nearly empty?
a : Its sharpness would wake the sleepiest muzzle. The second bite tastes much more like supper. | A scrap of firm fish with bread still makes a meal. The drawing can wait till afterwards.

scene riddle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know #riddle# about the one bit of cargo that gets lighter the more useful things you put on it.
b : A riddle about paper? | What's the answer?
a : A drawing of a shelf on a label. Every full crock in ink takes an empty place off my mind. | My little shelf sketch. It's a peculiar riddle because a different dock worker might give a different answer.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #frost.capitalize# shows me the places another pair of soles has tried already.
b : Do you follow? | Why like it?
a : After looking at how far the last shoe slipped. I'm fond of clear information on a cold plank. | Everything doubtful shines or leaves a plain mark. Warm damp can be remarkably discreet.

scene wind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wind.capitalize# gets right inside my grey muzzle fur and makes the skin pull.
b : Any shelter? | Hard to work?
a : Behind a high stack of casks for a short break. The load eventually goes and takes my wall away. | I manage. I still have the time and inclination to dislike it.

scene wait
when topic=work self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tide or a ship can keep a dock worker waiting without any intention of paying.
b : Do you fill the time? | Why stay near?
a : I draw in little shelf brackets. A good imagined pantry shouldn't sag under honest herring. | A lost lift is a lost bit of supper. Waiting gets more expensive once the work moves on.

scene crest
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A former place of mine went to better connections. I don't try to reproduce all the fine words that came with it.
b : Still angry? | Would you take that work back?
a : Careful. A quiet temper can preserve a good long memory without a great public performance. | I'd look at the offered wage and who's empowered to keep it. A crest alone gets no second vote.

scene homeblock
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry my spare tags up #self.street# in a dry fold of my cuff.
b : Do they fit the room? | Will you hang them up?
a : The drawings are larger than the larder. Both still fit in the same room for now. | One near the shelf I actually have. It's an honest comparison at supper.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# the drawer I've added beneath the pantry board.
b : For silver? | Where would it go?
a : For salt and two dry cloths. It seems sensible to imagine the ordinary parts properly first. | Under the shelf within reach when my free paw is carrying a crock.

scene prayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A short prayer before an opening barrel often concerns the safety of my toes.
b : Is that too small? | What about the cargo?
a : My toes matter to my work. The Bright One can judge their proper weight in a prayer. | Its owner's generally thought about it already. I'd still give thanks to get the whole thing safely ashore.

scene buy
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a shopkeeper who can say how much of the price is for an actual fish.
b : What else gets charged? | Do you argue?
a : The fancy label and the recommendation of a very fine name neither of us expects at supper. | I put my coin back if the account and the fish have drifted too far apart.

scene newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a stranger wants dock work directions I start by pointing out where the next load will land.
b : Before the office? | Does it move fast?
a : An unfamiliar face stands a better chance of reaching the tally without a barrel rolling through the introduction. | A wet round thing can be quite surprisingly ambitious compared with the wolf unloading it.

scene heights
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a room that lets me look down on a ship instead of always looking up at the sling.
b : Why the Heights? | Must it be grand?
a : A different first sight in the morning. I'd like the choice at least once in my life. | A stocked cupboard, a latch that holds and a roof the wind hasn't claimed. Those are grand conditions to me.

scene fishscale
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #scale# on a pantry sketch some nights so the crock shines like a real one.
b : Where from? | Superstitious?
a : A piece of herring I actually bought. I like my imagined future to contain some trace of today's honest supper. | Only careful about being entirely carried away by paper goods.

scene count
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I call a weight across the pier I want it heard clearly on the first calling.
b : How do you manage? | What if nobody hears?
a : Wait for a gap between loads. A quiet figure at the proper time goes a considerable distance. | I stay put till it's acknowledged. Otherwise a tidy account could leave somebody under a surprising weight.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed all the barrels in the bay came to rest as jars on the shelf I'd drawn.
b : Did the board hold? | What woke you?
a : The brackets began to squeak. I'd drawn them for a larder, not the contents of the harbour. | The thought of my ink cupboard losing half a city's supper. At breakfast I added another board underneath.

story labelstory [topic=memories]
  : I once drew my pantry straight across a cargo label without letting the old ink dry. My new high shelf soon acquired the address of a warehouse.
  : For an idle minute I pictured a whole warehouse where my supper belonged. Then I turned the scrap and drew a small crock instead.
  b : Was the small one enough?
  : I could imagine filling it for myself. A manageable ambition has quite a good flavour with bread.

story crockstory [topic=food]
  : The glaze chipped off a blue herring crock and left a clean white crescent. It began to look to me like a moon over the pantry boards.
  : It was only when the fish ran low that I could see a second chip inside. I took the two little moons as a plain reminder to save for another crock.
  b : Did you buy it?
  : I kept the fish in a smaller pot and put one coin aside. That's a real beginning, whatever colour the new moon will be.

story froststory [topic=weather]
  : A cargo tag rested on an icy cleat one morning. Lifted clear, its blank side had a beautiful white shelf pattern already laid out by the frost.
  : I tried to sketch round the lines. My warm paw arrived considerably faster than my pen, and most of the plan went back into water.
  b : Did anything stay?
  : One short bracket. I've copied it onto every decent pantry since, with a full crock above it if the day's gone well.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Roll it clear before saving the tag. | Watch the wet grain under that rim.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=full_larder
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Two firm brackets for a very full crock. | Draw the latch where a paw can reach.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=riddles
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a puzzle hiding behind that label. | One answer if the board stays level.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A clear print on the white edge. | Look where the last sole went sideways.

dlg @1 resident.hub : That's a spent cargo tag turned to its cleaner face. I've space left for a cupboard and a little while to hear your business.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor self.trade_words] : I'm #self.trade_words#. A landed barrel leaves a good deal less trouble than one with half its weight still swinging.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : A fresh account off the carrying boards. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's a new shelf on the drawing since you last passed the casks.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Something worth putting away on your top shelf.
graft resident.hub
choice What do you draw on the back of the freight label? -> label_pantry
node label_pantry
say My next larder. It'll be farther uphill than the shelf that held my supper last night. I can get a respectable row of pickle jars onto a small scrap.
free
choice What's the first thing you'd put on a real shelf? -> label_crock
choice Fine brackets under that drawing. -> hub
node label_crock
say One full crock of herring. Plans are pleasant, but I'd like the first supper in a higher room to taste of something I could carry there myself.
choice I'd keep room for a second crock. -> hub
choice Good lifting at the pier. -> bye
